From 8dc8fecad1f862898d9de00a39e9a72709b85d8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:04:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: the chapters of the chosen edition, and
 positions saved with their edition

With an edition of a Matroska file chosen before playback:

- The chapter list is that of the edition (CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::
  UseEditionChapters(), from what ffmpeg-9940 exports): its enabled
  chapters that are not hidden, by start, in file time; Kodi maps them to
  the time of the edition with the cuts and leaves out the ones that are
  cut, as it does with any cut. Without a chosen edition the list is the
  file's, as before.
- A disabled chapter of an edition that is not ordered is cut out too
  (RFC 9559: its content is skipped).

Kodi saves a position (resume point, bookmark) in the time of what plays,
the file without its cuts, and restores it with the cuts of the session
that restores it; with editions those can differ. For a file with two or
more editions to choose from, the player state that Kodi already saves
with resume points and bookmarks now names the edition that played
("<hadesmkvedition>UID</hadesmkvedition>", or "none"); no database field
changes. A position saved with another edition, or with none, is placed
in the file with the cuts it was saved with (those of that edition and of
any edit decision list file) and then plays from there: at the start of
playback, and for the seek of a bookmark (CGUIDialogVideoBookmarks sets
the state, then seeks). A position whose edition is not in the file, or
cannot be played, starts from the beginning. The same edition, a state
without the tag (positions saved before, discs, stacks) and files
without editions to choose from are restored as before. Stacks are not
asked which edition.

The arithmetic is that of CEdl::GetTimeWithoutCuts() and
GetTimeAfterRestoringCuts(), in MatroskaEditions.h with the chapter
list, the state tag and the placing of a saved position; its host test
has 110 checks, which 23 mutations make fail.
